+
+    <h2>1. Privacy by Design Architecture</h2>
+    <p>
+        <strong>The DevTools Times</strong> is engineered around <em>Privacy by Design and by Default</em> (GDPR Article 25). Privacy protections are built directly into our system architecture rather than bolted on after the fact:
+    </p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Zero-Tracking Default:</strong> All non-essential third-party scripts—including analytics and advertising networks—are disabled by default and never loaded unless you explicitly opt in via <a href="#privacy-preferences" data-manage-privacy="true">Manage Privacy Preferences</a>.</li>
+        <li><strong>First-Party Authentication:</strong> Account registration and sign-in are handled exclusively by first-party endpoints (<code>/api/auth/register</code> and <code>/api/auth/login</code>). Credentials are never transmitted to third-party cloud functions.</li>
+        <li><strong>Anonymous Cross-Origin Fetching:</strong> External fonts and media assets are requested using <code>crossorigin="anonymous"</code> and <code>referrerpolicy="no-referrer"</code> so that cookies and reading history are never leaked to external hosts.</li>
+        <li><strong>Cohort &amp; Topic Blocking:</strong> Browser-level interest profiling (<code>browsing-topics=()</code>, <code>interest-cohort=()</code>) is explicitly disabled across the entire origin via HTTP <code>Permissions-Policy</code> headers.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>2. Data Minimization Policy</h2>
+    <p>
+        In accordance with the principle of <em>Data Minimization</em> (GDPR Article 5(1)(c)), we collect and process only the minimum data strictly necessary to provide the requested functionality:
+    </p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Pseudonymous Accounts:</strong> Creating an account requires only a pseudonymous username ({DATA_MINIMIZATION_POLICY.minUsernameLength}–{DATA_MINIMIZATION_POLICY.maxUsernameLength} characters) and a password. We prohibit email addresses as usernames and reject any payload containing extraneous personal identifiers ({DATA_MINIMIZATION_POLICY.prohibitedUserFields.join(', ')}).</li>
+        <li><strong>Lazy Session Initialization:</strong> Anonymous visitors browsing articles do not have server-side session storage populated until they actively bookmark an article.</li>
+        <li><strong>Bounded Reading Lists:</strong> Reading lists store only validated article slugs (capped at {DATA_MINIMIZATION_POLICY.maxReadingListItems} items) and can be cleared with a single click.</li>
+        <li><strong>Minimized API Payloads:</strong> Public content APIs project only essential display fields (<code>{DATA_MINIMIZATION_POLICY.allowedArticleFields.join(', ')}</code>).</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>3. Secure Data Handling &amp; Cryptography</h2>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Password Hashing:</strong> Passwords are never stored or logged in plaintext. They are hashed server-side using memory-hard <code>scrypt</code> (N=16384, r=8, p=1) with a unique 16-byte cryptographic salt per user and verified via constant-time comparison (<code>crypto.timingSafeEqual</code>).</li>
